omx-contract (2.18.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 2.18.0: the hosting, LV2 and CLAP vocabulary
  * checks: every word in its place, every LV2 and CLAP term mapped, each
    rule with a red arm
  * docs: a specification's own term is named after its bundle, state.lv2
  * render: the vocabulary as a C header, a JSON Schema fragment and ts word
    lists
  * resource-profile, measurement: each word names the LV2 and CLAP terms it
    borrows its name from
  * formats/clap: every identifier of the 58 CLAP headers, mapped
  * formats/lv2: every term of the 24 LV2 specifications, mapped
  * inventory: a specification is named after its bundle, state.lv2
  * inventory: the LV2 and CLAP vocabularies as installed, written by a tool
  * resource-profile, machine-class: the words a host plans a plugin by, in
    the core
  * measurement: the words of the measurement format, in the core
  * hosting: every hosting code in the core, one file per dimension
  * test: the counts of data/ read from data/, its vocabulary apart from
    2.14.0's items
  * schema: the words and terms kinds, and the data directory laid out one
    domain per file

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:10:00 +0000
